5. The 0.4 benchmark's pictures

   Fifteen pictures: twelve museum works and three made with an image
   generator. bench/PICTURES.md has the same credits as a table. Each
   museum entry is copied from the museum's own record, read on
   23 November 2026: artist, title, date, medium, size, accession number,
   credit line, rights, link. Most of the full-size files are held outside
   this repository; the files that are in it are named in sections 1, 2
   and 4. Paintings of these pictures made by the painter follow section 3
   (museum works) or section 1 (Mittens and Kasha).

   Art Institute of Chicago. Its record marks each work public domain
   (is_public_domain: true); the museum releases images of such works
   under CC0. https://www.artic.edu/open-access/open-access-images

     Winslow Homer (American, 1836-1910), The Water Fan, 1898/99.
     Watercolor, with blotting and touches of scraping, over graphite, on
     thick, rough twill-textured, ivory wove paper. 37.4 x 53.4 cm
     (14 3/4 x 21 1/16 in.). 1972.190. Gift of Dorothy A., John A., Jr.,
     and Christopher Holabird in memory of William and Mary Holabird.
     https://www.artic.edu/artworks/38666

